Title: F2-M05 — The Empty Arsenal (briefing)
Credit: Staalfront
Author: Staalfront narrative team
Draft date: 2026-10-17

FADE IN:

INT. DRAINAGE CULVERT, SOUTH OF THE COMPOUND - NIGHT

[[AMBIENCE: dripping water, distant generator hum, boots shifting on wet concrete]]
[[MUSIC: muted, tense pulse]]

A hand-drawn plan of the compound is lit by a shuttered lamp. COMMANDER SAVA and LENKA crouch over it.

LENKA
(wary)
The enemy is supposedly stockpiling weapons at the arsenal. Our source says the shipments never arrived.

COMMANDER SAVA
(measured)
Then the arsenal may be bait. We need the ledger more than the ammunition.

[[SHOT: map]]
[[MAP: walled compound with south gate and two gun emplacements, guardhouse, motor pool, shed yard, archive building at the rear, generator, dry canal to the west with culvert into the wall]]

LENKA
Command's report lists three months of deliveries. A report is a clue. The invoices inside that archive are proof of whether a single crate ever came through the gate.

COMMANDER SAVA
(clipped)
The risks: two gate guns, a tank asleep in the motor pool, and a garrison that wakes the moment the alarm climbs. Eleven of us, two demolition charges, no base and no second team.

LENKA
The dry canal runs under the west wall. Nobody is shooting in there yet. The generator is on that side; kill it and the guns and the lights go together.

COMMANDER SAVA
(serious)
Save a charge for the way out. Once the alarm is up, they seal the canal and we are inside a box.

LENKA
(firm)
Infiltrate the compound, recover the payment records, and withdraw. Avoid destroying the archive building.

COMMANDER SAVA
(quieter)
And whatever name is on those invoices, Lenka, you tell me first. If it is not a Compact name, I want to know who we are actually fighting.

[[SFX: radio click]]
[[MUSIC: stop]]

FADE OUT.
